Google Apps Script Bridge

GAS acts as your middleware: it reads/writes Sheets and exposes endpoints to your React frontend via google.script.run (client-side) and doPost()/doGet() (for webhooks).

GAS responsibilities:

CRUD operations: Functions like addPlayer(data), updateRoster(id, data), deleteWaiver(id) that modify Sheets

Computed fields: Auto-calculate standings, player stats, seeding ranks on write

Validation: Check uniqueness, referential integrity, enum constraints before commit

Denormalization: When a persons.first_name changes, update all player_lookup rows with that person

Triggers: OnEdit/onChange triggers to sync cache tables and log status changes

Auth: Integrate with Google Sign-In; check user role from user_accounts sheet to gate features

Batch operations: Bulk imports from CSV (via bulk_import_staging sheet)

Example GAS stub:

function addGame(gameData) {
  const sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActive().getSheetByName('games');
  const newRow = [Date.now(), gameData.seasonId, gameData.divisionId, ...];
  sheet.appendRow(newRow);
  // Recalculate standings, update cache
  updateStandingsForDivision(gameData.divisionId);
  return { success: true, gameId: newRow[0] };
}

function getPlayersByTeam(teamId, seasonId) {
  const rosterSheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActive().getSheetByName('rosters');
  const data = rosterSheet.getDataRange().getValues();
  return data.filter(row => row[1] === teamId && row[2] === seasonId);
}


