Key Implementation Notes

Foreign Key Dropdowns: When a form needs team_id, use Data Validation → List with a formula referencing division_team_lookup sheet. Example: =FILTER('division_team_lookup'!C:C, 'division_team_lookup'!B:B=H1) // where H1 is the selected division_id

Caching in React: Load all teams, seasons, players once on app init, cache in Zustand/Context. GAS can push updates via Sheets change notifications or polling.

Unique Constraints: Sheets doesn't enforce DB-level uniqueness. Use GAS validation before insert. Example: rosters has a (team_id, player_id, season_id) composite key — check GAS before appending.

Computed Fields: Standings points, player stats, save %, goals_against_average — compute in GAS on game save, not in Sheets formulas (cleaner, faster).

Sensitive Data: Medical notes, emergency contacts, etc. were removed to match house-league scope. If you add them later, gate them behind admin roles in GAS.

Audit Trail: event_status_log tracks who changed what. GAS onEdit triggers should auto-log critical changes (waivers, transfers, game approvals).

